{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## PRODUCTION-STATE SMOKING GUN — the comment-ID dedup map is EMPTY\n\nDirect inspection of the live binding store on the `tickets` branch\n(`git show origin/tickets:.bridge_state/bindings.json`):\n\n```\ntop-level keys: ['bindings', 'comment_ids', 'reverse', 'version']\nbindings entries:      2475\ncomment_ids ENTRIES:      0     <-- empty\n```\n\n**Zero entries**, after thousands of comments have been successfully posted to Jira. The map is\npresent and structurally valid — it is simply never populated.\n\n### Why that is the whole story\n\n`_diff_comments` (`outbound_comments.py:405-445`) has two skips, and the code is explicit that\nthe first is PRIMARY and the second is only belt-and-suspenders:\n\n1. **PRIMARY — ID identity:** `binding_store.is_comment_mapped(local_comment_key)`\n   (`outbound_comments.py:411-415`). The docstring notes \"Identity is the key/ID, NOT the body —\n   so same-text comments never collide and an edited body is not seen as new.\"\n   **With `comment_ids` empty this skip can never fire for any comment on any issue.**\n2. **SECONDARY — body equality:** `compare_body not in jira_bodies`\n   (`outbound_comments.py:439`), described in-code as\n   \"a SECONDARY (belt-and-suspenders) skip behind the ID identity above — it guards a lost map\n   write (a crash between `add_comment` and `record_comment_id`'s save)\".\n\nThe intended safety net has become the *only* mechanism, and it is inherently lossy: it compares a\nlocally fitted+normalized body against bodies that have round-tripped through ADF/wiki\nconversion. The in-code comment at `outbound_comments.py:433-438` already concedes the rich path\ncan diverge on trailing whitespace.\n\n**This predicts exactly the per-issue variation observed, and it matches:**\n\n| Jira key | local comments | re-emitted/pass | matched by body | comment character |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| REB-424 | 25 | 3 | 22 | short/simple |\n| REB-1570 | 25 | 8 | 17 | mixed |\n| REB-1580 | 24 | 21 | 3 | rich |\n| REB-1861 | 40 | 39 | **1** | richest — avg 3.6 KB, heavy markdown |\n\nRich bodies fail the string-membership test and are re-posted forever; simple ones happen to match.\nNo uniform \"first N comments\" pattern fits this data, which rules out a pagination/truncation\nexplanation — and independently, the bug-1f3d pagination fix **is** present and correct\n(`acli_cli_ops.py:583-600` `get_comments` uses `--paginate`; `_parse_paginated_comments` handles\nthe multi-object stream; the snapshot truncation guard is at `outbound_comments.py:322-346`).\n\n### Relationship to the previously-fixed bug 1f3d-cb66-d3fc-4356\n\n`1f3d` (`florid-vigorous-urial`, closed) fixed the *pagination* route to this same 5000-comment\ninflation, and its cleanup task `bd80-0603-7d44-4d9f` purged duplicates from the 13 issues it had\ncapped. **This is the same failure class arriving through a different route** — the ID-map route —\nnot a regression of the pagination fix. Notably, `1f3d`'s fix hardened the SECONDARY skip's inputs\nwhile the PRIMARY skip was silently inert the whole time.\n\n### Remaining unknown — do NOT fix from static reading\n\n`comment_ids` is empty because `_record_comment_id`\n(`dispatch_apply_phases.py:309-334`) silently returns on any of four guards:\n`binding_store is None`; the entry has no `local_comment_key`; the `add_comment` result has no\n`id`; or the store lacks `record_comment_id`. Every one is a silent no-op by design, so nothing\nreports which fires. A fifth possibility is that `record_comment_id` writes but the map is never\npersisted/committed back to `.bridge_state/bindings.json`.\n\n**Which one it is must be established by instrumenting a live pass**, per this ticket's ACs. The\nempty map is proof the primary skip is inert; it is not yet proof of which guard causes it.\n\n### Precedent for the duplicate cleanup\n\n`bd80-0603-7d44-4d9f` is the established pattern for purging the duplicates once the loop is fixed\n— relevant for REB-1861's ~5000 and the other 27 affected issues."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787251802516868001,"uuid":"c1c6836a-367f-452a-bbc7-e271a54864d2"}